  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $100$ floors, so $n=100.$ We want to select $5$ of those floors for the elevator to stop, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{100}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{100!}{(100-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100!}{95!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100\\cdot 99\\cdot 98\\cdot 97\\cdot 96\\cdot \\cancel{95!}}{\\cancel{95!}5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{100\\cdot 99\\cdot 98\\cdot 97\\cdot 96}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\,034\\,502\\,400}{120} \\\\  & =75\\,287\\,520.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
